# Top-level direct dependencies for the GameVault Snake Edition launcher.
#
# This file is consumed by `uv pip compile` to produce the fully-locked
# `requirements.txt` (committed to the repo). End users install with:
#
#     pip install -r requirements.txt
#
# and get the same versions the CI builds against.
#
# To upgrade after editing this file:
#
#     uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#
# Why we list fewer packages than the old hand-written requirements.txt:
#
# - `darkdetect` is only imported inside `customtkinter`'s internals,
#   so it's a transitive dep of `customtkinter` and we don't pin it.
# - `jaraco.classes` / `jaraco.context` / `jaraco.functools` /
#   `more-itertools` are keyring's transitive deps. The keyring
#   version we pin below pulls the right versions in automatically.
# - `aiohttp`, `aiofiles`, `aiosignal`, `aiohappyeyeballs`,
#   `frozenlist`, `multidict`, `yarl` are pulled in by `pypdl`, which
#   is itself dead code (not imported anywhere in this project).
#   The aio* stack and `pypdl` have been removed.
# - `pySmartDL`, `pywin32-ctypes`, `win32-setctime`, `pypdl`, `loguru`,
#   and `patool` were not imported anywhere in the project. They were
#   left over from earlier versions and have been removed.
#   Note: `notify-py` (PyPI name) is imported as `notifypy` (module
#   name) in `bin/tabview.py`. The pip package name is `notify-py`.
# - `configparser` is in the Python stdlib since 3.0; not pinned.

# --- GUI framework ---
customtkinter
tkfeather
CTkMessagebox
CTkMenuBar

# --- Image handling ---
Pillow

# --- Auth / OS integration ---
keyring
notify-py

# --- HTTP ---
requests

# --- Paths / dates ---
platformdirs
dateparser
